    Good-enough starting point

    I removed all the existing perldoc from FastLook.pm :x
    need to look into those more since I need to learn to be
    more concise (and much more selective about what I want
    to explain...)

    I also didn't add the test files because they were
    originally meant for List::BisectSearch, which was like
    a fraction of this interface (with left search only,
    no search-any variants either); the NEW stuff with
    syntactic sugar and arybase (Array::Base) compatibility
    and everything definitely needs to be tested too,
    which -- agh, i'm going to re-organize as well....

    I'm not sure if this is too much comments for non-POD
    stuff.  I tried my best to make every comment fit on
    one screen so it's not conceptually too overwhelming.
    I see the point of separating user-level docs, which
    enjoys more abstraction and less nitty-gritty details;
    but at the same time, I find it difficult to read the
    code itself due to how clean it is in contrast!
    I hope this has the effect of bridging the gap between
    the two layers, so everyone has something to look at
    when descending the hierarchy of abstraction.

